00:01:27.345 --> 00:01:30.825
So when naming different molecules
found in general chemistry, we follow a

00:01:30.825 --> 00:01:36.615
systematic naming process, which is also
known as the IUPAC Convention for naming.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.090
This is something we do
in general chemistry.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:43.050
In organic biochemistry, we like
to follow a set of rules so that

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:47.130
